Source --> IMPORT
User --> ARCHIVAL
User --> TRANSMISSION
User --> REVIEW
User --> DELIVER

ARCHIVAL ..> IMPORT : <<include>>
ARCHIVAL ..> ASSEMBLE : <<include>>
ARCHIVAL ..> REVIEW : <<include>>
ARCHIVAL ..> METADATA : <<include>>
ARCHIVAL ..> NORMALIZE : <<include>>
ARCHIVAL ..> VALIDATE : <<include>>
ARCHIVAL ..> INTEGRITY : <<include>>
ARCHIVAL ..> PACKAGE : <<include>>

TRANSMISSION ..> IMPORT : <<include>>
TRANSMISSION ..> ASSEMBLE : <<include>>
TRANSMISSION ..> REVIEW : <<include>>
TRANSMISSION ..> FORMAT : <<include>>
TRANSMISSION ..> DELIVER : <<include>>

EDIT ..> ASSEMBLE : <<extend>>
MARKUP ..> ASSEMBLE : <<extend>>
OPTIMIZE ..> FORMAT : <<extend>>
SECURITY ..> TRANSMISSION : <<extend>>

PACKAGE --> Destination
Destination --> Archive
DELIVER --> Destination
Destination --> Recipient
DELIVER ..> STATUS : <<include>>

note bottom of ASSEMBLE
  Archival and transmission share document assembly,
  but remain separate user goals with different
  validation, metadata, packaging, and delivery concerns.
end note
@enduml
